{
  "operators": [
    {
      "name": "custom_multihead_attention",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "query",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "key",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "value",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "in_proj_weight",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[3*embed_dim, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "in_proj_bias",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[3*embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": true,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "out_proj_weight",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[embed_dim, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "out_proj_bias",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": true,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "embed_dim",
          "kind": "int",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "num_heads",
          "kind": "int",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "need_weights",
          "kind": "bool",
          "default": true,
          "optional": true,
          "nullable": false
        },
        {
          "name": "average_attn_weights",
          "kind": "bool",
          "default": true,
          "optional": true,
          "nullable": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "type": "tuple",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": "tensor",
            "dtype": "torch.float32",
            "device": "cuda",
            "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]"
          },
          {
            "type": "tensor",
            "dtype": "torch.float32",
            "device": "cuda",
            "shape": "[batch, seq_len, seq_len]"
          }
        ]
      },
      "semantics": [
        "Computes MultiheadAttention forward with default settings (no masks, no causal). Inputs are sequence-first (seq_len, batch, embed_dim).",
        "Performs in_projection via in_proj_weight (3*embed_dim, embed_dim) and in_proj_bias (3*embed_dim) to produce q,k,v. Then reshapes for heads: (seq_len, batch*num_heads, head_dim). Computes scaled dot-product attention: attn = softmax((q @ k^T)/sqrt(head_dim)) @ v. Then out_projection with out_proj_weight and out_proj_bias.",
        "need_weights=True returns both attn_output [seq_len, batch, embed_dim] and average attention weights [batch, seq_len, seq_len] averaged over heads (average_attn_weights=True). The second tensor's shape is (batch, seq_len, seq_len), matching reference checkpoint step_001.",
        "All computations in float32; no padding masks; no dropout (training=False)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "custom_cat",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "t1",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "t2",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "dim",
          "kind": "int",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "type": "tensor",
        "dtype": "torch.float32",
        "device": "cuda",
        "shape": "[seq_len, batch, 2*embed_dim]"
      },
      "semantics": [
        "Concatenates t1 and t2 along dim=-1 (last dimension), producing output with last dim doubled. The two inputs are identical in this usage (attn_output concatenated with itself), general cat should handle arbitrary shapes along dim.",
        "Order of tensors preserved: first t1 then t2 along dim. Output shape is [seq_len, batch, 2*embed_dim]."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "custom_glu",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "x",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[seq_len, batch, 2*embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "dim",
          "kind": "int",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "type": "tensor",
        "dtype": "torch.float32",
        "device": "cuda",
        "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]"
      },
      "semantics": [
        "GLU splits x along dim=-1 into two halves a and b of equal size, then computes a * sigmoid(b). Output has last dim embed_dim (half of input).",
        "The split is exactly first half and second half along dim; no broadcasting needed. Sigmoid computed elementwise."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "custom_linear",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "x",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[seq_len, batch, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "weight",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[linear_out_features, embed_dim]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": false,
          "optional": false
        },
        {
          "name": "bias",
          "kind": "tensor",
          "dtype": "torch.float32",
          "device": "cuda",
          "shape": "[linear_out_features]",
          "layout": "supports strides",
          "nullable": true,
          "optional": false
        }
      ],
      "returns": {
        "type": "tensor",
        "dtype": "torch.float32",
        "device": "cuda",
        "shape": "[seq_len, batch, linear_out_features]"
      },
      "semantics": [
        "Performs linear transformation y = x @ weight^T + bias. x has shape (..., embed_dim), weight is (linear_out_features, embed_dim), bias is broadcast over leading dims.",
        "In this task, x is [seq_len, batch, embed_dim], output is [seq_len, batch, linear_out_features]. Bias is added if provided (reference linear.bias exists)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "reference_steps": [
    {
      "checkpoint": "step_001",
      "source": "attn_output, _ = self.attention(query, key, value)",
      "semantics": [
        "Returns tuple (attn_output [1024,16,256], attn_weights [16,1024,1024]). attn_output is the result of MultiheadAttention with default settings; attn_weights average over heads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "checkpoint": "step_002",
      "source": "x = torch.cat((attn_output, attn_output), dim=-1)",
      "semantics": [
        "Concatenates attn_output with itself along last dim, producing [1024,16,512]."
      ]
    },
    {
      "checkpoint": "step_003",
      "source": "x = self.glu(x)",
      "semantics": [
        "Applies GLU along dim=-1: splits [1024,16,512] into two halves [1024,16,256], computes a * sigmoid(b), output shape [1024,16,256]."
      ]
    },
    {
      "checkpoint": "step_004",
      "source": "x = self.linear(x)",
      "semantics": [
        "Linear transformation: y = x @ linear.weight^T + linear.bias, output [1024,16,128]."
      ]
    },
    {
      "checkpoint": "step_005",
      "source": "return x",
      "semantics": [
        "Final output tensor shape [1024,16,128], float32, CUDA."
      ]
    }
  ]
}